==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Twintail Medusa Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Naga Cat''' when obtained from [[Okame's Teahouse (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Medusa Cat is an extremely situational anti-Relic. Although freezing them sounds like a great unit, her low uptime and mediocre procs mean you have to stack her to freeze Relics consistently. This is, however, not worth it, as her low health means she'll just die quickly.

[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] is more reliable than this unit. Although Medusa Cat has higher health, Area Attack, better range and an [[Immune to Curse|Immunity to Curse]], Rodeo Cat is slightly cheaper, has shorter cooldown to be stacked more, and has faster attack rate.

She is only useful against [[Oldhorn]], [[M. Ost]], [[Idi:Re]] and [[Relic Bun-Bun]] since she outranges them. Her matchups against other Relics are poor, since they can invade her blindspot and kill her right away. Be careful when using her against [[Idi:Re]], as her extreme damage will kill Medusa Cat in one attack, instantly wiping out your stack.

==='''True Form'''===
Naga Cat improves her HP, Freeze chances, and Freeze duration. The extra HP might not be that much, but it does somewhat help with stacking. On that note, the improved odds and duration of her Freeze ability only really become useful with a stack of Naga Cats, allowing her to more consistently get a Freeze off and keep it on long enough for the next Freeze to proc, she is now worth using to permafreeze Relic enemies, especially when you don't have [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]]. She is also much more reliable than [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ultra Delinquent Cat]] due to her overall better consistency.

Once [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] is obtained, Naga Cat becomes an obsolete unit, however, she still can be used with him as a supplemental anti-Relic. Overall, a below average True Form, but is situationally amazing regardless.
